Change notice (Apache-2.0 section 4(b)): this package redistributes no
upstream file. What it carries are short excerpts and paraphrases,
re-formatted into a different document and annotated in Chinese by this
skill's author, together with repository file:line locators. Where upstream
material has been abridged or reworded, that is stated at the point of use.
No upstream file is therefore modified in place; this paragraph is the change
notice for every excerpt taken from an Apache-2.0 source.

Apache-2.0 sources: as required by Apache-2.0 sections 4(a) and 4(c), a copy
of the Apache License 2.0 is included at licenses/Apache-2.0.txt, and the
copyright and attribution notices retained from those sources are reproduced
in the NOTICE file distributed with this package. Where an upstream project
ships its own NOTICE file, the attribution notices it contains are reproduced
in full in that NOTICE file, as required by Apache-2.0 section 4(d).

MIT-licensed sources: the copyright notices retained from those sources, and
the common MIT permission notice, are reproduced in NOTICE and at
licenses/MIT.txt.

BSD 3-Clause sources: a copy of the BSD 3-Clause licence text is included at
licenses/BSD-3-Clause.txt, and the copyright notices retained from those
sources are reproduced in NOTICE. BSD 3-Clause is permissive, not copyleft —
it adds only a no-endorsement clause (clause 3) on top of MIT, and this skill
honours that clause. The two sources it covers are both mixed-licence
repositories; the per-package breakdown is in NOTICE.

Licence scope inside mixed-licence sources: two upstream repositories are not
uniformly covered by a single licence, and this skill quotes only the parts
named in the table above.

  - zhu1090093659/dsh-web — Apache-2.0 at the root; BSD-3-Clause in
    packages/dsh-{community-plugins,doctor,plugin-manager} and in one skin
    directory. Four further skin asset directories are CC BY-NC-SA 4.0
    (non-commercial). This skill reproduces nothing at all from those skin
    asset directories: only repository-root material and `packages/` sources
    are quoted, as set out in references/10a.

  - yjh051108/dsh-routing-suite — self-inconsistent. Its root LICENSE is MIT,
    while its package.json files declare BSD-3-Clause (root, injector/) and
    Apache-2.0 (graded/), and injector/ ships no LICENSE file at all. This
    skill applies the BSD-3-Clause terms to injector/ material, since they
    carry strictly more obligations than MIT, and the Apache-2.0 terms to
    graded/ material. The per-file breakdown is in NOTICE.

A note on AGPL sources: this package cites no AGPL-licensed project. One such
source had been used by references/10b-casebook-tools.md; it was removed from
the cited set on 2026-09-16, with its generic lessons restated as the author's
own advice. See the removal list at the end of that file's section 1.2.

